  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "A new name at the top",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "social-2108577347192676612"
      ],
      "text": "Yi-Chia Chen took the ARC-AGI-3 public lead with 59.17%, ahead of Tufa Labs at 56.52%. ARC Prize announced the change, and the closing board confirms the order. The observed score event shows Chen moving from 55.77% and second place to the lead; the record does not establish a reliable previous-evening team comparison for her. Tufa also improved, from an observed 55.89% to 56.52%, even as the lead changed hands. These are public standings, with the final private result still to come."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The chase tightens",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "mtg jumped from seventh in its earlier tracked observation to third at 44.32%, a verified gain of 5.99 points. NVARC3 reached 40.97% and stood fifth at the close; the score-event record shows its climb from 37.51%, although its previous-evening comparison is unavailable. Majkel1337 held fourth at 42.66%, with the last dance 🕺 sixth at 39.30% and dreach.ai seventh at 39.11%. Nhan Duc Nguyen moved from 19th at the prior evening observation to eighth at 38.84%."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Experience across the field",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-roster-0",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-roster-1",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-archive-0",
        "person-david-hartmann-archive-0",
        "person-jan-disselhoff-archive-0"
      ],
      "text": "The public NVARC3 roster lists Ivan Sorokin and Jean-François Puget’s verified cpmpml account. ARC Prize credits both with the 2025 NVARC championship; that historical result belongs to the earlier team and season. Lord Han Solo stood 13th, while David Hartmann and Jan Disselhoff were farther down this ARC-3 board. Hartmann and Disselhoff were credited on the ARChitects’ 2025 runner-up team, but they are separate 2026 entries here."
    },
    {
      "heading": "More movement below",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "social-2108463895128269084"
      ],
      "text": "AFF AI CLUB climbed to 27th at 33.92% and ERS to 57th at 33.08% in the prior-evening comparison. The keithtyser entry was 69th at 32.74%; its score was unchanged in the available comparison. Tufa Labs posted a playful message about its position earlier in the day. It is competition banter, not evidence of the team’s hardware, spending or approach."
    }
